# --- upstream checkouts (our forks) -------------------------------------------
# The three repositories we patch (harbor, SWE-bench, the Terminal-Bench 2 task
# set) are cloned, never vendored into this history: their branches are the source
# of truth and `scripts/export_bench_patches.sh` exports the diffs into
# benchmarks/patches/ so the changes stay reviewable here.
# Rooted at the repository: an unanchored `harbor/` also swallows
# benchmarks/patches/harbor/, i.e. the exported diffs this comment is about.
/harbor/
/SWE-bench/
/terminal-bench-2-1/
/vendor/
# A nested checkout has its own history; keep its packed objects out regardless.
/harbor/.git/
/SWE-bench/.git/
/terminal-bench-2-1/.git/

# --- benchmarks ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Run artifacts, cached datasets, container build contexts and generated
# predictions are large or machine-specific; nothing here belongs in the repo.
benchmarks/runs/
# Summary CSVs / analyser output: machine-specific numbers belong next to the run
# that produced them, not in the repository (the *method* is what is tracked).
benchmarks/results/
benchmarks/datasets/
benchmarks/.cache/
benchmarks/**/build_context/
*.predictions.jsonl
predictions.jsonl
runs/
